# T12/T27 QLoRA training container recipe (Apptainer definition).
#
# STATUS: recipe_only_not_built. This file documents the intended contents of
# a separate training container so a live build is reproducible when it is
# actually approved and run on the cluster (see
# configs/environments/t12_cluster_training.json -> container_recipe).
#
# This recipe MUST NOT be used to rebuild, replace, or overwrite the pinned
# vLLM inference container (vllm-openai-v0.20.1.sif, see
# configs/environments/t12_cluster_inference.json). Inference and training
# environments are and remain separate containers.
#
# Base image is pinned to the same CUDA 13.0 / PyTorch 2.11.0 combination
# already verified live for the inference container so the two stacks stay
# CUDA-driver compatible on the same cluster nodes, even though they are
# built and stored as distinct .sif files.

Bootstrap: docker
From: pytorch/pytorch:2.11.0-cuda13.0-cudnn9-runtime

%labels
    RECIPE_ID t12_training_container_v1
    TICKET T27
    ROLE training
    DEVELOPMENT_ONLY true
    NOT_THE_INFERENCE_CONTAINER true

%post
    set -e
    python3 -m pip install --no-cache-dir \
        "transformers==5.7.0" \
        "peft==0.18.0" \
        "bitsandbytes==0.48.1" \
        "accelerate==1.11.0" \
        "safetensors==0.7.0" \
        "datasets==3.6.0"

%environment
    export HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1
    export TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1
    export VLLM_WORKER_MULTIPROC_METHOD=spawn

%help
    T12/T27 QLoRA smoke/training container recipe (planned, not yet built).
    Adds peft/bitsandbytes/accelerate on top of the pinned PyTorch/CUDA base
    used by the inference container, without touching the inference SIF.
    Build only after cluster/container-build approval; this .def file alone
    does not create a live .sif artefact.
